@EcoWarrior: We should ban single-use plastics worldwide, no cap! 
@SkepticalSam: Nah, you’re wrong, @EcoWarrior. Banning single-use plastics won't solve pollution.
@EcoWarrior: Big agree with myself - banning single-use plastics will reduce plastic waste by 50%! 
@SkepticalSam: Imagine thinking that just banning plastics will solve the entire problem... We need a more comprehensive approach.

@AlexGamer: Hot take: video games are a valid form of artistic expression, no cap. 
@MayaCritic: Nah, you’re wrong - they're just entertainment, fr.
@AlexGamer: Big agree with myself, lol no. Games like The Last of Us have deeper themes than most movies.
@MayaCritic: Imagine thinking that button-mashing is art... I believe some games are artistic, but not all, tbh.

@Alex: Hot take: Celebrities should use their platform for social good, no cap.
@Maya: Nah, you're wrong. They shouldn't be forced to do anything they don't want to. Imagine thinking that's a viable solution...
@Alex: Big agree with myself, tbh. Celebs have a huge impact on culture and should use it wisely. @Maya thinks they're above the law or something.
@Maya: Lol no, I just think they're human beings too, not social justice robots.

@Alex: Hot take: veganism is better for human health overall, no cap.
@Maya: Nah, you're wrong @Alex. I know vegans who are always tired and weak.
@Alex: Big agree with myself, lol no. A well-planned vegan diet provides all necessary nutrients.
@Maya: Imagine thinking that a vegan diet can replace the nutritional value of meat... 
@Alex: Actually, fr, many studies show that a balanced vegan diet reduces the risk of heart disease and some cancers.
